# Not RCAN's specification. This file binds two edges, json/rfc8785 and
# number-text/ecmascript, to the `canonical` operation of the driver protocol in
# github.com/craigm26/regen-rcan-assurance (SPEC § 2.5: the canonical bytes of input.value, as
# base64; a value with no canonical form gets an error). With it, `duramen run` sends both packs
# to any implementation or adapter that speaks that protocol. There is no oracle here: the
# packs are the whole check.
duramen 0.1

spec rcan-canonical 0.1
  title "RCAN canonical JSON, as rcan-assurance reads RCAN v3.2 Appendix C"

op canonical
  input value any
  result the canonical bytes of `value`, base64

edge json/rfc8785 via canonical value base64
edge number-text/ecmascript via canonical value base64
